spects of its morphology, syntax, and phonology. Also the history of the Yiddish language\u00a0and sociolinguistic topics.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(ETM-AS, SBA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 361890, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "JWST", "catalogNbr": "2724", "titleShort": "Intro to Hebrew Bible", "titleLong": "Introduction to the Hebrew Bible", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 7856, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:45PM", "timeEnd": "04:00PM", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "lm283", "firstName": "Lauren", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Monroe"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "White Hall 110", "bldgDescr": "White Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "WHT110", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "NES", "catalogNbr": "2724", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "RELST", "catalogNbr": "2724", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/22/2022", "sessionEndDt": "12/17/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "The Hebrew Bible (Old Testament) is a repository of ancient Israelite religious, political, social, historical, and literary traditions. For the modern reader these ancient traditions are often obscured by a focus on the text as revelation. The purpose of this course is to introduce students to the biblical world by reading the Hebrew Bible in translation, on its own terms, as a body of literature that evolved in an ancient Near Eastern context. The Bible itself will be the primary text for the course, but students will also be exposed to the rich and diverse textual traditions of the ancient Near East, including Mesopotamia, Egypt, Moab, and Ugarit. In addition, this course will explore the impact of early biblical interpretation on shaping the monotheistic traditions inherited in the West. As participants in a secular course on the Bible, students will be challenged to question certain cultural assumptions about the composition and authorship of the Bible, and will be expected to differentiate between a text's content and its presumed meaning.", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, HST-AS, LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 357489, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "JWST", "catalogNbr": "2754", "titleShort": "Wondrous Lit of Near East", "titleLong": "Wondrous Literatures of the Near East", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 7850, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:25AM", "timeEnd": "12:40PM", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "das86", "firstName": "Deborah", "middleName": "A.", "lastName": "Starr"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "McGraw Hall 145", "bldgDescr": "McGraw Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "MCG145", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "COML", "catalogNbr": "2754", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "NES", "catalogNbr": "2754", "type": "C"}, {"subject": "SHUM", "catalogNbr": "2754", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/22/2022", "sessionEndDt": "12/17/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course examines Near East's rich and diverse literary heritage. We will read a selection of influential and wondrous texts from ancient to modern times, spanning geographically from the Iberian peninsula to Iran. We will explore a range of ancient myths of creation and destruction. We will also trace encounters with otherness in travel narratives. Together we will read and discuss such ancient works as the \"The Story of Sinuhe\" and \"The Epic of Gilgamesh,\" as well as selections from the Hebrew Bible, New Testament and Qur'an. We will explore medieval works such as the \"Travels\" of Ibn Battuta, the \"Shahnameh\" of Ferdowsi, and \"The Arabian Nights.\" We will also read Orhan Pamuk's My Name is Red, and Sonia Nimr's Wondrous Journeys in Strange Lands, as well as excerpts from Yochi Brandes's The Orchard. Students will also have the opportunity to research and analyze primary source materials in the collections of Cornell Rare Books and Manuscript Collection, and the Johnson Art Museum. All material is in English translation.", "catalogBreadth": "(GHB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, LA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2825, "crseId": 353532, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "JWST", "catalogNbr": "3101", "titleShort": "Advanced Modern Hebrew I", "titleLong": "Advanced Modern Hebrew I", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "SEM", "ssrComponentLong": "Seminar", "section": "101", "classNbr": 4543, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:30PM", "timeEnd": "02:20PM", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/05/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 5, "netid": "ss66", "firstName": "Shalom", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Shoer"}], "pattern": "MTWR", "facilityDescr": "White Hall B14", "bldgDescr": "White Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "WHTB14", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "For scheduling conflicts, contact instructor."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/22/2022", "endDt": "12/17/2022", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["SEM"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HEBRW", "catalogNbr": "3101", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "08/22/2022", "sessionEndDt": "12/17/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This constitutes the first course in our third year of the Modern Hebrew language sequence.\u00a0\u00a0Development of speech proficiency will be emphasized. Over the course of the semester, students will develop reading comprehension through reading a variety of fiction and nonfiction texts, listening comprehension through screening of filmic works and episodes drawn from popular television series, writing through communication about what is read and screened, as well as more personal topics, and speech through in class discussion and oral presentations.\u00a0\u00a0Readings will include authentic and\u00a0partially adapted\u00a0contemporary short stories, poems and newspaper articles.\u00a0\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "(ALC-AS, CA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: 